[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Sold Out]
[00:13.95]When will the writer see the play?
[00:19.55]'The play may begin at any moment,' I said.
[00:25.35]'It may have begun already,'
[00:28.07]Susan answered.
[00:30.75]I hurried to the ticket office.
[00:34.19]'May I have two tickets please?' I asked.
[00:39.05]'I'm sorry, we've sold out,' the girl said.
[00:44.93]'What a pity!' Susan exclaimed.
[00:49.15]Just then,
[00:50.43]a man hurried to the ticket office.
[00:54.66]'Can I return these two tickets?' he asked.
[00:59.75]'Certainly,' the girl said.
[01:04.17]I went back to the ticket office at once.
[01:09.05]'Could I have those two tickets please?' I asked.
[01:13.58]'Certainly,' the girl said,
[01:16.84]'but they're for next Wednesday's performance.
[01:20.03]Do you still want them?'
[01:23.59]'I might as well have them,' I said sadly.
